LLM proposes to modify file: 'train_svm.py'
Explanation: The current model uses the default regularization parameter (C=1.0) implicitly in LinearSVC. In high-dimensional, sparse text classification settings such as TF-IDF on user chat data, unconstrained or high C values can lead to overfitting on rare n-grams and noisy annotations, decreasing test F1 performance and requiring more solver iterations.
Rationale: Setting C = 0.5 provides stronger L2 regularization, which enlarges the margin and prevents the decision boundary from overfitting to high-frequency or idiosyncratic tokens in the toxic chat dataset. Mathematically, smaller C emphasizes margin maximization over slack variable penalty minimization, leading to improved generalization across unseen test distributions and faster convergence during dual coordinate descent optimization.

